WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.210
It's always sad to watch your favorite character
shuffle off this mortal coil.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.790
But it's even worse for the actors involved,
who often have to film these emotionally difficult

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:09.570
scenes over and over again.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.219
It's no wonder, then, that actors often try
to lighten the mood by goofing off right as

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:15.000
their character is kicking the bucket.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.270
Here's a look at some unexpected bloopers
during death scenes.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.210
Inglourious Basterds

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.420
Sally Menke was an Academy Award-nominated
film editor who worked on nearly all of Quentin

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.360
Tarantino's films until she passed away in
2010.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.020
While working with Menke, actors and crew
members on Tarantino films would leave friendly

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.510
messages for her while shooting — which
she'd discover months later in the editing

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:37.839
bay, like this bit from Inglorious Basterds
actor Til Schweiger.

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:38.839
"Sally!

00:00:38.839 --> 00:00:40.409
I am not dead!

00:00:40.409 --> 00:00:41.960
I just pretended.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:48.309
Now I'm gonna go after him and I'm going to
kick his f---ing Nazi b---s, okay?"

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:50.109
Dracula: Dead and Loving It

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:54.920
Mel Brooks virtually created the movie parody
genre, making full-length parodies of entire

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.499
film genres like Blazing Saddles, Spaceballs,
and Dracula: Dead and Loving It.

00:00:59.499 --> 00:01:03.379
In one scene, a pair of vampire hunters played
by Brooks and Steven Weber needed to stake

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.989
a vampire named Lucy.

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:08.659
Weber barely held it together as the scene
plays out a little more… vigorously than

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:09.740
he expected.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.000
"Ohhhh my God!"

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.810
The Avengers

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.890
All true fanboys and fangirls shed a tear
at the shocking loss of SHIELD agent Phil

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.049
Coulsen in Marvel's blockbuster The Avengers.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:30.820
But nobody took it quite as hard as Cobie
Smulders, whose agent Maria Hill simply expressed

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.180
what every one of us was feeling in that dreadful
moment.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.520
"Coulsen!

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.480
Nooooo!

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:37.740
God!

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.040
You were the greatest man I ever knew!"

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.159
And she didn't stop there.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.250
"You will be avenged!

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.580
You will be avenged!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:53.100
I will get The Avengers, and you will be avenged,
Coulsen!"

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.100
Jaws

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:59.350
As grizzled old Quint in Jaws, Robert Shaw
got to have a spectacular, gruesome, and memorable

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:00.350
farewell.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.770
The cast and crew probably had no idea the
scene would go down in the annals of movie

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:08.440
history, because to Shaw it was downright
hilarious...thanks to just a little too much

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:09.440
fake blood.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.340
Calling Mel Brooks!

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:17.760
[Groaning then laughter]

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:21.080
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.610
Making movies is tough work, with shooting
days regularly lasting more than 14 hours

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:27.930
as crews prepare sets, lighting, props, and
practical effects rigs.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:31.940
That means a lot of tired actors, as Michael
Rooker proved in this scene from Guardians

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.520
of the Galaxy volume 2.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.550
Since he was playing the deceased Yondu, all
he had to do was lie there while his co-stars

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:41.989
delivered a heartfelt eulogy over his body,
but it turned out to be… just a little too

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:42.989
comfortable.

00:02:42.989 --> 00:02:48.120
"Sometimes it's right there by your side all
along and you don't even know it."

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.540
[Snoring]

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.800
Even Drax couldn't wake him!

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.560
[Snoring]

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.930
Merlin

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:03.140
Eoin Macken portrayed Sir Gwaine on the long-running
British series Merlin — right up until the

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.930
character was laid low by treachery.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:09.090
The once mighty Gwaine expired in the arms
of his friend Percival, played by Tom Hopper,

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.680
while sadly lamenting his failure to stop
the bad guys.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.620
Or at least, it should have been sad, but
Hopper apparently took it a little differently.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:25.160
[Laughter]

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.420
The Interview

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:31.310
In Seth Rogen and James Franco's controversial
2014 comedy The Interview, the duo played

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:35.409
an American talk show producer and host sent
to North Korea on a mission to assassinate

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:37.579
the nation's leader, Kim Jong Un.

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:41.209
Along the way, Rogen's character got into
a fight to the finish with a North Korean

00:03:41.209 --> 00:03:42.209
agent.

00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:45.260
But as this blooper shows, the two actors
weren't exactly treating it like a moment

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.020
where life hangs in the balance.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.340
"Slow push!"

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.420
[Screaming]

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.120
"Sorry!"

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.159
Game of Thrones

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:57.090
When Jon Snow was assassinated on Game of
Thrones by his own men at the end of season

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:01.099
5, it was one of the most shocking moments
ever on the HBO fantasy series.

00:04:01.099 --> 00:04:06.120
So would the red witch be able to bring him
back to life during season 6?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.120
Thanks for watching!

